    "No real browser, CSS layout/overflow, screenshot, native touch-hit, accessibility-tree or deployed-route tests were performed here. DOM/Canvas harness validates script/event semantics only.",
    "UI-event witness coverage samples levels 1, 50 and 100 per game; all 3,000 engine witnesses and input schemas were checked.",
    "Fixed-policy witnesses establish solvability against shipped normal AI, not adversarial forced wins, uniqueness or optimality.",
    "Constant-policy checks sample 70 combinations in each of 400 corrected levels, not all real-valued inputs. Some introductory motocross and sports levels still admit simple winning inputs; no tested constant policy defeats every level in their game.",
    "Normalized numerical/geometry uniqueness is not a proof of 100 distinct topologies. The games intentionally reuse rules and use parameterized physical scenarios.",
    "Physics and rules are documented arcade simplifications. Parking collision uses coarse body proxies, and not every edge case of real-world sport rules is modeled.",
    "Progress is local convenience storage, not authenticated anti-cheat. Sports saves progress/assistance, vehicles also resume input sessions.",
    "Two of 1,500 one-frame vehicle perturbations did not win; this is not a claim of unique solutions. Every game has independently observed alternate valid controls."
